<title>SOUTH AFRICA: DORBYL BUYS CONTROLLING SHARE IN STALCOR.</title>
<headline>DORBYL BUYS CONTROLLING SHARE IN STALCOR.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dorbyl Ltd said on Tuesday its steel division, Baldwin Steel, bought a controlling share in Stalcor, an official distributor for Columbus Stainless and Hullet Aluminium.</p>
<p>The price of the purchase was not disclosed. Dorbyl said the acquisition was in line with its strategy to penetrate the high growth stainless steel and aluminium markets.</p>
<p>The partnership would complement Baldwins Steel's core business of stocking and processing carbon steel products, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
